@startuml

' =============================================================
' UC-005 Design Class Diagram (PIM) - English
'
' MDA Level: Platform Independent Model
' Perspective: Specification / Analysis (Design without platform)
'
' Derived from:
' - uc-005.dm.pim.puml (entities)
' - uc-005.ssd.pim.puml (system operations)
' - uc-005.oc.pim.md (operation contracts)
'
' This DCD shows the system's INTERNAL structure at PIM level.
' It assigns responsibilities to classes using GRASP patterns
' (Information Expert, Controller, Pure Fabrication) but does NOT
' commit to any platform, framework, or layered architecture.
'
' Compare with PSM DCD which adds:
' - .NET types (Guid, Task<T>, IEnumerable<T>)
' - Clean Architecture layers (Domain, Core, Infrastructure, etc.)
' - EF Core entities and DbContext
' - REST controllers and HTTP semantics
' - Dependency injection interfaces
' =============================================================

title UC-005 Design Class Diagram — Phone List Coordination (PIM)

skinparam classBackgroundColor #E6F4FF
skinparam classBorderColor #4682B4
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' --- Entities (from PIM Domain Model) ---

class "Caregiver" as Caregiver <<entity>> {
    + id : UUID
    + firstName : String
    + lastName : String
}

class "Phone" as Phone <<entity>> {
    + number : String
}

class "PhoneAssignment" as Assignment <<entity>> {
    + id : UUID
    + assignedAt : DateTime
    --
    + getPhoneNumber() : String
    + getCaregiverName() : String
    + getShiftType() : ShiftType
}

enum "ShiftType" as ShiftType <<enumeration>> {
    Day
    Evening
    Night
}

' --- System operations (from Operation Contracts) ---

class "PhoneCoordinationSystem" as System <<system>> {
    + getPhoneListForActiveShift() : List<PhoneAssignment>
    + selectShift(shiftType : ShiftType) : List<PhoneAssignment>
    + assignPhone(phoneNumber : String,\n  caregiverName : String,\n  shiftType : ShiftType) : PhoneAssignment
    + clearAssignment(phoneNumber : String,\n  shiftType : ShiftType) : void
    + refreshPhoneList() : List<PhoneAssignment>
}

' --- Domain associations ---
Assignment "1" --> "1" Caregiver : assigned to
Assignment "1" --> "1" Phone : for phone
Assignment "1" --> "1" ShiftType : during shift

' --- System composition ---
System "1" o-- "0..*" Assignment : manages
System "1" *-- "7" Phone : owns
System "1" o-- "0..*" Caregiver : knows

' --- Notes ---
note right of System
    <b>GRASP: Controller pattern</b>
    PhoneCoordinationSystem acts as the entry point
    for all system operations from external actors.

    <b>One operation per OC contract:</b>
    Each method corresponds to one Operation Contract
    in uc-005.oc.pim.md.
end note

note bottom of Assignment
    <b>GRASP: Information Expert</b>
    PhoneAssignment owns the knowledge of who carries
    which phone on which shift. It exposes that
    knowledge via getter operations.
end note

note as N1
    <b>PIM-level design constraints:</b>

    - All types are platform-independent (UUID, String, DateTime, List<T>)
    - No async semantics (PIM is synchronous specification)
    - No persistence concerns (no repositories, no DbContext)
    - No architectural layers (Clean Architecture is PSM-level)
    - No interfaces for DI (introduced only when needed by PSM)

    Marks for PIM-to-PSM transformation are added in a
    separate file: uc-005.dcd.pim-marked.puml
end note

note as N2
    <b>What about Slottet?</b>

    Slottet exists in CIM as the business domain context.
    At PIM level, Slottet is implicit — it IS the system.
    The PhoneCoordinationSystem represents Slottet's
    capability to coordinate phones.

    If multiple facilities were modeled, Slottet would
    reappear as an entity. For UC-005 single-facility
    scope, it is not needed.
end note

@enduml
